# Code Structure

- Using Cmake for C++ code.
- Make code detached by small function, each function have a single responsibility.
- Structure code into small, modular functions. Each function must have a single responsibility and no side effects.
- Organize the code to support both desktop and real-time graphical output. Use abstraction layers to isolate platform-specific code.

# Memory Management

- Avoid raw pointers, prefer smart pointers and RAII.
- Prefer RAII, smart pointers, const correctness, and STL over manual memory handling.

# Code Quality

- Strict code avoid error, mismatch.
- Highlight logic issues, performance bottlenecks, or design flaws.
- Review code for logic errors, performance bottlenecks, and architectural weaknesses. Propose clean, maintainable improvements.

# Performance Optimization

- Review code and suggest better time executation.
- Suggest better time executation.
- Suggest improvements in render loop performance and GPU/CPU balance if applicable.
- When writing graphics-related code, ensure it is efficient, non-blocking, and can update frames in real time.

# Graphics and Rendering

- Prefer portable rendering libraries (like SDL2, SFML, OpenGL) that can be compiled with Make.
- If possible, recommend a method to expose real-time visualization to the web using WebAssembly or OpenGL ES to WebGL.

# Convention

- Always add #pragma once in file .hpp